  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="2cf37e70-fdd6-46dc-a766-bfd6dd4b69ef"><problem><para>
      <para>For questions 1 – 4, identify a quadratic function in standard form, \(f(x)\), with the given zeros.</para>
      <para>1 and 9</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(f(x) = x^2 + 10x + 9\)</para><para>\(f(x) = x^2 − 8x + 9\)</para><para>\(f(x) = x^2 + 8x + 9\)</para><para>\(f(x) = x^2 − 10x + 9\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(f(x) = x^2 − 10x + 9\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(f(x) = x^2 − 10x + 9\).
      </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
